  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "game-description-50e9bf32-1234-4249-a7e0-131a030cb95f-0",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "html": "Magic: The Gathering combines a card game with the construction of the deck used to play it. Lands provide mana, which pays for creatures, spells, and other effects; players seek ways to overcome an opponent’s defenses and win, often by reducing their life total to zero. Timing and interactions between cards can turn a small change in the board into a major advantage."
    },
    {
      "id": "game-description-50e9bf32-1234-4249-a7e0-131a030cb95f-1",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "html": "Richard Garfield designed the game, first published by Wizards of the Coast in 1993. Its expandable card pool supports many formats, so the permitted cards, deck-building restrictions, and multiplayer arrangements depend on the version being played."
    },
